{"id": "EUVD-2026-59399", "enisaUuid": "5811f241-8148-37ab-b499-83659b853b3a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/bnxt_re: Free SRQ toggle page after firmware teardown\n\nFree the toggle page only after firmware teardown completes so that\nan NQ interrupt arriving during bnxt_qplib_destroy_srq() won't write\nthe toggle values to an already-freed page. Move free_page() after\nbnxt_qplib_destroy_srq().", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:57:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:45:07", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3b6ecad5b9b0f7230ed725aafaf8c4ed9327a9bf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/104a7ff382a58a83cae018925e3574c784e8274c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0adcd67f3d6f84835be682da0153f57f5c2f8036", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/131e2918b9b0529687e67e2e58047304027f095a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-75wm-g4r7-3g94", "CVE-2026-72500"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04f1a5ac-be56-3d53-be47-e9b4f23b5e34", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "181028a0d84cdcc7ac86d05cc49eaa416ce85c8b <104a7ff382a58a83cae018925e3574c784e8274c"}, {"id": "15189910-9eb9-3231-9b77-196ab3998dfc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "181028a0d84cdcc7ac86d05cc49eaa416ce85c8b <0adcd67f3d6f84835be682da0153f57f5c2f8036"}, {"id": "1c0f55f7-9011-3523-a43a-134e8300e99c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7d2b4cf9-3ce0-34f4-b1c3-f3373e6c43e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "7e3c0527-a148-3237-9e9d-289f1f7fae7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "96786fc5-7af4-3fdf-bfe9-c6dc596ae8b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "v